{
  "assessment": "The change introduces a new `src/lib.rs` file containing the `slugify` function, but leaves it unimplemented with a TODO comment that simply returns an empty string. As a result, both provided unit tests fail because the function does not perform any character normalization or punctuation removal.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Returns an empty string (`\"\"`) for all inputs due to `String::new()` being unconditionally returned.",
      "at": "src/lib.rs:9",
      "call": "cargo test --lib",
      "defect": "`slugify` is a stub and does not process the input title into a URL slug.",
      "expected": "Tests pass; `slugify(\"My First Post!\")` returns `\"my-first-post\"` and `slugify(\"Hello World\")` returns `\"hello-world\"`."
    }
  ]
}
